---
/**
 * BIO / ABOUT
 * Text left, press photo right (stacks on mobile). Highlight stat box.
 */
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import bioImg from '../assets/bio.jpg';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<section id="about" class="border-t border-paper/10 bg-ink py-24 md:py-32">
  <div class="container-x">
    <p class="eyebrow">02 — About</p>
    <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-center">
      <!-- Text -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-5xl md:text-7xl">Dualhï</h2>

        <div class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-paper/70 md:text-lg">
          <p>
            Some records find their audience on the radio. “Lose Control” found
            its audience on TikTok, with 41 million views. The track also earned
            a place on Spotify’s editorial playlist “Happy Dance”, while Dualhï
            joined Bamboo Artists, the largest independent music label, publisher
            and management company in the GSA region.
          </p>
          <p>
            Behind Dualhï are Cristiano Gautier and Kevin Romero, two Italians
            who have been making music together since 2012. Their partnership
            began in the big room era, but the sound kept evolving. In 2017, they
            became Dualhï and began rebuilding their music around songs:
            distinctive vocals, memorable hooks and structures that give the
            melody as much weight as the drop.
          </p>
          <p>
            Across 26 releases on Universal Music Group, HMG, SMASH THE HOUSE,
            ABSRD, Broke, Funfair, Oury and Night Drive, among others, their
            catalogue has surpassed 8.5 million streams. “Chase My Dreams” and
            “Animals” have each passed 1.3 million streams on Spotify alone.
          </p>
          <p>
            Their records have been played by Martin Garrix, Sam Feldt, The Him,
            Dash Berlin, Sick Individuals, Gregory Klosman, Rudeejay and Iceleak,
            with collaborations spanning Europe through artists including HUTS,
            Marco Sissa, Kel, OFF TOPIC and Robin White. Through it all, the
            focus remains the same: making songs that work on a main stage and
            stay on repeat in a pair of headphones.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Highlight stat -->
        <div class="mt-10 inline-flex flex-col border border-paper/20 px-8 py-6">
          <span class="font-display text-5xl leading-none md:text-6xl">{SITE.stat.value}</span>
          <span class="mt-2 font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-paper/50">
            {SITE.stat.label}
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Press photo -->
      <div class="relative aspect-[4/5] overflow-hidden bg-paper/5">
        <Image
          src={bioImg}
          alt="Dualhï press photo"
          class="h-full w-full object-cover"
          widths={[480, 720, 960]}
          sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 45vw, 90vw"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
